# Rust statistical handwriting and per-glyph controls

## Scope and existing evidence

Implement typed manual statistics for height, width, spacing, baseline, slant,
roundness, ink, texture, per-glyph shape and variation context in Rust, reusing
existing bounds.

## Practical acceptance — 2026-11-03

**Basis:** tested native Rust statistics and executable CLI/browser controls,
not a theoretical-only completion. The finite v1 target is **bounded numeric
statistics**, not glyph outlines or calibrated pen strokes.

- `atrament_handwriting_statistics` owns ten exact dimensions: height,
  width, letter spacing, baseline offset, slant, roundness, flattening,
  ink thickness, pressure and texture. All have Rust-enforced bounds.
- Each global dimension and exact per-grapheme override accepts minimum,
  maximum, mean, median and standard deviation. NFC and NFD remain distinct.
  The CLI and local browser submit proposals to the same Rust JSON codec.
- `preview_value` uses an exact seed, grapheme and occurrence key for
  reproducible **numeric estimates**. It does not preserve calibrated moments
  or draw strokes. Unavailable ink/shape/joins are labeled as unavailable
  in the browser and README, not represented as generated ink.

**Accepted:** the live Firefox/Rust local-file journey saves an exact `ñ`
height override (2600..3400 µm, mean 3100, median 3000, deviation 60)
with seed `18446744073709551615`, reopens it from the Rust server,
replays a numeric preview with the maximum occurrence key, and restores the
numeric and slider values. Domain/CLI tests also cover globally edited
statistics, repeatability, and NFC/NFD differences.

**Refused:** a mean of 99999 µm fails without modifying the saved JSON.
Other domain tests refuse inverted limits, impossible deviations, repeated
dimensions, and invalid/multigrapheme identities.

**Evidence:** `cargo test --offline -p atrament_handwriting_statistics
-p atrament_handwriting_statistics_json -p atrament_profile_editor_cli`
(18 domain, 8 codec, 27 CLI tests); real headless Firefox test
`Firefox edits, saves and reopens both profiles through Rust localhost` in
`tests/browser/workspace/adapter-inbound/runtime-frame-ancestors.mjs`.

**Still unavailable:** actual per-letter stroke geometry, contextual forms,
writer calibration, true target moments, complete glyph coverage, and ink
rendering. Those cannot be inferred from a numeric preview. P4-012 and P5-011
remain open executable tasks; this acceptance does not close them.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for bounded native numeric statistical editing and
  deterministic estimates; test-owned Linux browser/CLI evidence, 2026-11-03.
- **Delivered:** ten bounded variables, exact per-glyph overrides, numeric
  preview, native file round-trip, an accepted example and a refused update.
- **Not delivered:** authentic handwriting strokes, calibrated moment
  distributions or context-dependent shaping (P4-012/P5-011 remain open).
